Milestone 1: freeze the kernel

Our immediate mistake would be trying to canonicalize everything. Instead define a minimal executable kernel.

I would currently nominate:

# PANTHEON_KERNEL.yaml
version: "0.1.0"
invariants:
  - preserve_provenance
  - preserve_uncertainty
  - distinguish_inclusion_from_acceptance
  - confidence_must_not_exceed_evidence
  - reality_response_is_information
  - failed_routes_remain_recoverable
  - transformations_must_record_loss
primitives:
  differentiate:
    purpose: "Create useful distinctions."
    class: primitive
  omega:
    name: Everything Operator
    purpose: "Restore excluded/rejected/unknown material to consideration."
    class: primitive
  transform:
    name: Topological Transduction
    purpose: "Change representation while preserving selected invariants."
    class: primitive
  attract:
    name: Recurrent Attractor Synthesis
    purpose: "Stabilize useful recurring structures."
    class: primitive
  prune:
    name: Entropy Pruning/Renewal
    purpose: "Remove low-value complexity without destroying recoverability."
    class: primitive
  project:
    name: Differential State Projection
    purpose: "Estimate useful state deltas and futures."
    class: primitive
derived:
  indigo_hammer:
    uses:
      - differentiate
      - transform
      - attract
    purpose: "Extract reusable invariants across renderings."
  metamap:
    uses:
      - project
      - attract
    purpose: "Learn which routes work for which problem classes."
  kintsugi:
    uses:
      - omega
      - differentiate
      - transform
    purpose: "Recover value from failure."
  santa_compiler:
    uses:
      - omega
      - project
      - metamap
    purpose: "Increase downstream agency and useful branching."
experimental:
  - lucky_nozzle
  - operator_wrestling_mat
  - mnemonic_homeostasis
  - gift_engine

Important: “experimental” does not mean weak. It means not yet promoted by benchmark evidence.

That gives us an evolutionary pressure:

\text{Experimental}
\xrightarrow{\text{measured contribution}}
\text{Derived}
\xrightarrow{\text{irreducibility}}
\text{Primitive}

No concept gets promoted just because we like it.

